Base: cursor/c03-route-action-transport-e504 @ 9220bfab0b30ecc74c8911c199efcd71461271ee
Branch: cursor/c03-route-session-wire-e504

DO NOT APPLY this hunk. Do not edit App/AppSession.swift, App/AppCompositionRoot.swift, or Questify.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj from this branch.

The installed read is still one GET /api/play/route-action. This branch does not send a second request. `serviceResult` is not an argument and is not a network read.

The action id and the route session id are the ones already stored on the current completion journal (`cachedCompletion.intent.advance.actionID` and `cachedCompletion.intent.routeSessionID`) or, when that journal does not have both, on the current completion receipt (`reward.routeActionId` or `reward.actionId`, and `reward.routeState.sessionId`, `reward.themeRuntime.sessionId`, or `reward.sessionId`). `PlayExperienceCoordinator.heldRouteActionIdentity` reads that pair. `App/PlayExperienceView.heldRouteActionRead` passes the pair to `PlayRouteMapView`. If either id is absent, the read stays closed. This does not mint an action id or a session id, and it does not fill a missing id from the live route snapshot.

currentMemberId, AppUser.userId, and Account.id are the same member. The member id is `account.id` only. Do not invent another member id. Do not use a staff id.

An unknown approval refuses the send. Do not borrow the older `.playNodesAndRouteState` grant, `playReadConfiguration`, or `PlayReadRoute` (`api/play/nodes`, `api/play/route-state`) to open `api/play/route-action`.

No new file is added. No new PBX file reference is required. Do not edit pbxproj.

